 admitted past the mechanism-delta ratchet by a '# mechanism-ok: test_helper' marker, which must name a sunset ticket that retires it (src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py). This ticket is that sunset. The helper builds real <name>.exe launchers (distlib ScriptMaker) so PATH-stubbed tools run on Windows; that is a second process layer per stub and a dev-extra dependency on distlib.\n\n## Retirement path\nTests that stub git, scc, acli or sandbox-exec could intercept the spawn in-process instead, the way tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py::test_a_slow_local_git_call_does_not_fail_the_repair_pause wraps rebar._store.gitutil._run_in_group. That works where the spawn goes through one rebar seam in the test process; it does not reach child processes (tests/interfaces/metrics_polyglot_support.py runs the CLI as a subprocess; tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py stubs git for a nested pytest). Retiring the helper therefore needs either a spawn seam those children honour, or a decision that the helper is permanent infrastructure (then close this as wontfix only after repointing or removing the marker).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] tests/_exe_stub.py and its mechanism-ok marker are removed with every caller ported, and the distlib dev-extra entry is dropped, OR the marker is repointed to a ticket that records a decision to keep the helper.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e37b-2ac1-c998-4fb3","ticket_type":"task","title":"Retire tests/_exe_stub.py: intercept tool spawns in-process instead of PATH stubs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0b0fb7cd-2d36-49c1-ab4d-8a6eebfa2c36","03114ea5-3f60-476b-8468-74d